# SICE Project UI Agent Rules  
*For Smart Inventory, Smart Experience — leveraging Shadcn MCP, Rive, Lottie, Spline, ShaderGradient, Icon8, and 21st.dev.*

---

## 1. General Principles

- Core UI structure should be built using **Shadcn MCP server components/blocks** whenever available.
- Use advanced animation/design tools (**Rive, Lottie, Spline, ShaderGradient, Icon8, 21st.dev**) to add microinteractions, 3D visuals, dynamic backgrounds, icons, and modern UI polish.
- Always maintain **accessibility**, **responsiveness**, and **theming consistency** in all UI elements.
- Never manually hard-code UI components that exist as MCP blocks unless customization cannot be done with MCP.

---

## 2. Planning & Component Mapping

- For each new feature or screen, list all UI needs in the UX plan (`ux-structure.md`).
- Map every feature to:
  - The best matching **Shadcn MCP block/component**.
  - Additional tools needed for advanced visuals or animations.
- Maintain a feature-to-component-and-tool mapping in project documentation.

---

## 3. Component & Integration Rules

### A. Shadcn MCP

- Use MCP API exclusively to:
  - List components/blocks.
  - Preview demos.
  - Retrieve and insert UI code.
- Prefer blocks (composite UI pieces) over atomic components.
- Insert static UI structure first, then wire event/data logic.

### B. Advanced Visual & Animation Tools

- **Rive**: Animate buttons, badges, avatar states, and microfeedback. Embed as React components inside MCP containers.
- **Lottie**: Use for onboarding, notifications, and loading animations. Place Lottie components within or alongside MCP blocks.
- **Spline**: Embed 3D scenes for product views, dashboards, and spatial data. Anchor within MCP layouts.
- **ShaderGradient**: Implement dynamic background gradients and moods with CSS/custom components. Bind to live app state.
- **Icon8**: Use systematic SVG icons for nav, badges, and status indicators. Animate icon states based on interaction/data.
- **21st.dev**: Use accessible and trendy components (cards, forms, inputs) as supplements or replacements when suitable.

---

## 4. Motion State & Live Data Integration

- Implement a global motion state store (Zustand or Redux) to synchronize UI animations and live data-driven visual changes (stock alerts, chat activity, theme shifts).
- Connect WebSocket/API events to trigger animations across MCP and external visual components.

---

## 5. Demo & Insert Workflow

- Always preview components/blocks via MCP demo endpoint before inserting.
- Confirm suitability visually and functionally.
- Insert generated code only after approval.
- Document notes about feature-specific usage and integration for team clarity.

---

## 6. Accessibility, Theming & Responsiveness

- Components and integrated tools must follow WCAG guidelines.
- Support light/dark mode theming out-of-the-box.
- Ensure full responsiveness across devices.
- Document any necessary overrides or exceptions.

---

## 7. Version Control & Team Practices

- Keep this rule file and UX structure docs versioned alongside source code.
- Update rules as the product or tech stack evolves.
- Make onboarding documentation to help new team members understand these guidelines.

---

## 8. Example Feature-Component-Tool Mapping Table

| Feature           | MCP Block/Component     | Additional Tools            | Notes                                    |
|-------------------|------------------------|-----------------------------|------------------------------------------|
| Product Card      | `product-card-block`   | Rive, Icon8, ShaderGradient | Animated buttons, stock warning badges   |
| Inventory Chart   | `dashboard-table`      | Spline, Lottie              | 3D pulse & onboarding animations         |
| Add/Edit Modal    | `modal`, `form`        | ShaderGradient, 21st.dev    | Gradient backgrounds, animated inputs    |
| Chatbot           | `chatbot-block`        | Rive, Icon8                 | Animated avatar and status icons         |
| Stock Alert       | `alert`                | Lottie, Icon8               | Confetti animations, pulsing badges      |

---

## Final Note

- Follow these rules strictly when generating UI with AI agents.
- Balance MCP usage for structure with rich integration of animation tools for best user experience.
- Continuously improve the rules as your project and tools evolve.

---

